.TH std::inplace_vector::shrink_to_fit 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::inplace_vector::shrink_to_fit \- std::inplace_vector::shrink_to_fit

.SH Synopsis
static constexpr void shrink_to_fit() noexcept;  (since C++26)

Does nothing.

Nominally, this function is a non-binding request to decrease capacity so that the
internal storage contains only size() elements. However, such a request is always ignored
by the fixed-capacity container std::inplace_vector<T, N>.

.SH Parameters

\fI(none)\fP

.SH Return value

\fI(none)\fP

.SH Complexity

Constant.

.SH Notes

This function exists for compatibility with vector-like interfaces.

